'''Gabriel Sîncrăian''' (born 21 December 1988) is a [[Romania]]n [[weightlifter]] who competes in the 85&nbsp;kg weight division.

==Career==
He took part in the [[Weightlifting at the 2012 Summer Olympics – Men's 85 kg|2012]] and 2016 Olympics and won a bronze medal in the same [[Weightlifting at the 2016 Summer Olympics – Men's 85 kg|85-kg]] event in 2016.<ref>{{ Cite sports-reference abriel Sîncrăian{{cite web|url=https://www.sports-reference.com/olympics/athletes/si/gabriel-sincraian-1.html |title=Gabriel Sîncrăian Bio, Stats, and Results &#124; Olympics at Sports-Reference.com |accessdate=2012-08-02 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20121217052010/http://www.sports-reference.com/olympics/athletes/si/gabriel-sincraian-1.html |archivedate=2012-12-17 }} | 3 = 11 August 2012}}</ref> Sîncrăian won two more medals at the European championships in 2012 and 2016.<ref>[http://www.iat.uni-leipzig.de/datenbanken/dbgwh/daten.php?spid=068B4219C1FA435096866F111E3090FC Sincraian Gabriel (ROU)]. iat.uni-leipzig.de</ref>

On 13 October 2016, the [[International Weightlifting Federation|IWF]] reported that Sincraian had tested positive for excess testosterone in a test connected to the Rio Olympics, and he was stripped of the medal.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.espn.com/olympics/story/_/id/17783940/romanian-weightlifter-gabriel-sincraian-lose-bronze-medal-failed-rio-olympic-drug-test|title=Weightlifter Gabriel Sincraian fails Rio Olympic drug test|date=October 13, 2016|publisher=Associated Press|accessdate=2016-10-14}}</ref>

In November 2020, the reanalysed doping tests from the 2012 Summer Olympics turned out positive for [[metenolone]] and [[stanozolol]] as well.<ref>[https://stillmedab.olympic.org/media/Document%20Library/OlympicOrg/IOC/Who-We-Are/Commissions/Disciplinary-Commission/2020/ITA-LD-LRTII-2718614-IOC-Disciplinary-Commission-Decision.pdf International Olympic Committee Disciplinary Commission Decision], [[International Olympic Committee]], 23 November 2020.</ref>

In 2022 the [[International Weightlifting Federation]] annulled his results between 3 August 2012 and 17 January 2022. <ref>https://ita.sport/sanction/international-weightlifting-federation-iwf/</ref>
